{"title":"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangular field is 300 feet wide and 400 feet long. Random sampling indicates that there are, on the average, three ants per square inch through out the field. [12 inches = 1 foot.] Of the following, the number that most closely approximates the number of ants in the field is \n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/e/bfe0697ad39cd8f32a0e93d23364cd85e85b26cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ \\text{500 thousand} } \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ \\text{5 million} } \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ \\text{50 million} } \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ \\text{500 million} } \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ \\text{5 billion} }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"668\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The rectangular field is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcffd40d29b8ffbcb35f7e64471261e1ff002220.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$300 \\text{ feet} \\cdot \\frac{12 \\text{ inches}}{1 \\text{ foot}} =  3600 \\text{ inches}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"253\" height=\"37\" /> wide and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/3691430c0e56233f0948225cbfe56950b3cbfd3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$400 \\text{ feet} \\cdot \\frac{12 \\text{ inches}}{1 \\text{ foot}} =  4800 \\text{ inches}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"253\" height=\"37\" /> inches long.\n</p><p>It has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c42fe326243c734a3fc661fe0d05987daa7eb5bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.6\\cdot 10^3 \\cdot 4.8 \\cdot 10^3 = 17.28 \\cdot 10^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"240\" height=\"15\" /> square inches. \n</p><p>We multiply by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to account for the ants to get approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8b3248953d6ff81ad765dab47fdfd00aa4602a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50 \\cdot 10^6$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/6/906734e2f1010e9a171ffee8050cbc0649cea37c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> million <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/b/f4bc0f7a1bdf6ce2928f7efd015f88a9afe77cea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME\" title=\"1995 AHSME\">1995 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1995 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1995\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1995_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1995 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?t